title = "[P2] Align Autobahn newHeads test fixture with committed-block hash validation"
revision = "bb8caac8b3e73e3e2f4b330805574f0bcb540641"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "TestSubscribeNewHeadsAutobahn still publishes the unrelated hash and header values at rpc/subscribe_test.go:140 and rpc/subscribe_test.go:181 and expects them at rpc/subscribe_test.go:210 before reaching rpc/subscribe_test.go:222, whereas rpc/setup_test.go:381 serves the block defined at rpc/setup_test.go:270 with the different hash from rpc/setup_test.go:91 and header from rpc/setup_test.go:187, so the consumer at rpc/subscribe.go:165 rejects it at rpc/subscribe.go:643 under the validation introduced by commit 0bdbbf4a9afba2badd9cddf2594a1b4209e82e89."
close_comment = "The positive Autobahn newHeads fixture uses a hash and header values that differ from the committed block. The follow-up test repair will align those values and verify that mismatched events are rejected while subsequent valid heads still arrive."

